;=================================================
; 412, 勉強
;---------------------------------------
; 法力の勉強というものがピンとこないので読経と写経にした
;=================================================
;==================================================
;Optional: Determines if the standard description should be skipped.
;Return 0 if description and KOJO should be shown, 1 if description should be hidden and KOJO shown, 2 if description should be shown and KOJO hidden, and 3 if both description and KOJO should be hidden.
;==================================================
@M_KOJO_MESSAGE_MESSAGECHECK_COM_K88_412
RETURN 1

@M_KOJO_MESSAGE_COM_K88_412
CALL M_KOJO_MESSAGE_COM_K88_412_1
RETURN RESULT

@M_KOJO_MESSAGE_COM_K88_412_1
LOCAL = 1
IF LOCAL
	;sutras were replaced, but it's alright
	IF ABL:MASTER:教養 > ABL:教養
		PRINTFORMW 「No ignorance, no ignorance, no old age nor death...」
		PRINTFORMW Kyouko seems to be chanting sutras without knowing their meaning, so you teach her more about them.
		PRINTFORMW How would it be like for a yamabiko to obtain the power of Buddhism?
		PRINTFORMW ...Maybe she could put deadly curses on those that reply to her greetings?
	ELSEIF ABL:MASTER:教養 / 2 == ABL:教養 / 2
		PRINTFORMW 「Hey-hey, how do you spell this?」
		PRINTFORMW You try to write sutras together with her, but it seems Kyouko is struggling to read the complicated words.
		PRINTFORMW It may be that as a yamabiko, as a being that imitates sounds, she will always have a problem with it.
		PRINTFORMW But even an amateur would like the letters, the sounds and the meanings to make sense together.
	ELSE
		PRINTFORMW 「All-is-well-that-ends-well!」
		PRINTFORMW You study by repeating the sutras Kyouko is reciting.
		PRINTFORMW Sometimes when you recite a sutra Kyouko recites the same one again unintentionally, so it's a bit difficult to make progress.
	ENDIF
ENDIF
RETURN 1

